    {
      "at": "2026-11-05T18:20:17Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R1-F1",
      "reason": "The helper gives the program a fixed environment with no proxy variable, so a proxy around the helper cannot see its traffic. Increment E now runs the program directly with the helper environment plus loopback proxy variables, states that only a seen connection is proof, and tries the operating system sandbox as a second probe."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-05T18:21:55Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F1",
      "reason": "A probe cannot prove that nothing is sent, so the plan no longer depends on it. Increment E now finds the program own off switch in its source, sets it in the helper environment with a test whatever a probe sees, and records what the probes could and could not observe. If the source names no switch the question is reported as open."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-05T18:22:41Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F1",
      "reason": "The proxy probe ran without confinement, so a client that ignored the proxy variables could have connected outside the machine. Both probes in Increment E now run inside the operating system sandbox that allows only the loopback address, after a canary shows an outside address is refused; without the canary no probe is run."
    }
  ],
